# Restart Mission sends MISSION_SET_CURRENT 0, and the vehicle goes back to the start.
#
# BUTrestartmission_Click is setWPCurrent(sysid, compid, 0). The mission is first moved on to item
# 3 with Set WP, so a vehicle already at 0 cannot pass the test by standing still; SITL answers
# each with MISSION_CURRENT. `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:1891-1905`
#
# Needs SITL: tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-restartmission.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
# The setup writes a five-item mission to SITL through its second port, 5762.

setup printf 'QGC WPL 110\n0\t1\t0\t16\t0\t0\t0\t0\t-35.363262\t149.165237\t584.09\t1\n1\t0\t3\t22\t0\t0\t0\t0\t0\t0\t10\t1\n2\t0\t3\t16\t0\t0\t0\t0\t-35.3629\t149.165237\t10\t1\n3\t0\t3\t178\t0\t5\t0\t0\t0\t0\t0\t1\n4\t0\t3\t16\t0\t0\t0\t0\t-35.3625\t149.1657\t10\t1\n' > $WORK/mission.waypoints
setup cargo run -q -p mp-cli --bin headless-planner -- mission tcp:127.0.0.1:5762 $WORK/mission.waypoints

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 8

# The Actions grid is on the Actions page, tabActions; the strip opens on Quick, as
# tabControlactions.SelectedIndex = 0 has it. `GCSViews/FlightData.Designer.cs:595-611`
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click fly-tab-actions
expect fly.tab tabActions

# Item 0 is home and goes to the Home Location boxes, not the rows; with the boxes empty,
# processToScreen asks "Reset Home to loaded coords" (GCSViews/FlightPlanner.cs:5640-5660) and
# the question is modal, as the C#'s message box is. Yes takes the home, as an operator would.
click tab-plan
click plan-read
expect plan.prompt Reset Home Coords
click plan-prompt-ok
click tab-fly

click fly-setwp-list
click fly-setwp-4
click fly-setwp
expect vehicle.mission_current 4

click fly-restartmission
expect fly.sent MISSION_SET_CURRENT seq=0
# Item 0 is home, not something to fly to: ArduCopter answers a set to 0 with MISSION_CURRENT 0
# once and then streams its first navigation command, 1 here. Measured against this SITL with
# pymavlink - set 2 streams 2, set 4 streams 4, set 0 streams 1.
expect vehicle.mission_current 1
